('IE:civil-engineer:2026-09-12:wave-a-v1','IE:civil-engineer','shortage_signal',array['ie-civil-engineer-shortage-signal-1'],array['IE:civil-engineer:shortage_signal:wave-a-v1'],12,'career-opportunity-v4-foundation','available','proxy','medium','SOLAS lists the combined national group ''Civil engineers & construction project managers'' as a shortage.','government_aggregator','medium',0.8,'SOLAS lists the combined national group ''Civil engineers & construction project managers'' as a shortage.',null,'proxy'),
('IE:civil-engineer:2026-09-12:wave-a-v1','IE:civil-engineer','vacancy_intensity',array['ie-civil-engineer-vacancy-intensity-1','ie-civil-engineer-vacancy-intensity-2'],array['IE:civil-engineer:vacancy_intensity:wave-a-v1'],4,'career-opportunity-v4-foundation','available','proxy','medium','2025 survey explicitly names site/civil engineers; 2024 evidence also named civil/site engineers. The fallback remains broader than a clean vacancy-rate statistic.','government_aggregator','medium',0.8,'Conservative fallback: low vacancy intensity (3) + one persistence point (1). The survey confirms repeated difficult-to-fill mentions but cannot support a vacancy-rate band above low without a denominator.',null,'fallback'),
