('IE:construction-manager:2026-09-12:wave-a-v1','IE:construction-manager','shortage_signal',array['ie-construction-manager-shortage-signal-1'],array['IE:construction-manager:shortage_signal:wave-a-v1'],12,'career-opportunity-v4-foundation','available','proxy','medium','SOLAS lists the combined national group ''Civil engineers & construction project managers'' as a shortage.','government_aggregator','medium',0.8,'SOLAS lists the combined national group ''Civil engineers & construction project managers'' as a shortage.',null,'proxy'),
('IE:construction-manager:2026-09-12:wave-a-v1','IE:construction-manager','vacancy_intensity',array['ie-construction-manager-vacancy-intensity-1','ie-construction-manager-vacancy-intensity-2'],array['IE:construction-manager:vacancy_intensity:wave-a-v1'],4,'career-opportunity-v4-foundation','available','proxy','medium','2025 survey explicitly names project/site managers; 2024 evidence also named project/site managers. No occupation-level denominator is published.','government_aggregator','medium',0.8,'Conservative fallback: low vacancy intensity (3) + one persistence point (1). The survey confirms repeated difficult-to-fill mentions but cannot support a vacancy-rate band above low without a denominator.',null,'fallback'),
('IE:construction-manager:2026-09-12:wave-a-v1','IE:construction-manager','industry_diversity',array['ie-construction-manager-industry-diversity-1'],array['IE:construction-manager:industry_diversity:wave-a-v1'],1,'career-opportunity-v4-foundation','available','proxy','medium','SOLAS publishes main-sector shares for the broader construction occupational family, not this exact Career. Residual employment is aggregated into one ''other'' bucket as a conservative concentration upper bound.','government_aggregator','medium',0.8,'Published shares cover 91% of the occupational family; the remaining 9% is deliberately treated as one sector. The resulting score must be labelled Estimated and must not be described as an exact Career HHI. Component normalized_value stores the derived 0–5 diversity points; HHI remains separately preserved as derivedHhiUpperBound for provenance.',null,'derived'),
('IE:construction-manager:2026-09-12:wave-a-v1','IE:construction-manager','employment_momentum',array['ie-construction-manager-employment-momentum-1'],array['IE:construction-manager:employment_momentum:wave-a-v1'],1.2,'career-opportunity-v4-foundation','available','proxy','medium','Uses the combined civil engineer/construction project manager growth series.','government_aggregator','medium',0.8,'Uses the combined civil engineer/construction project manager growth series.',null,'derived'),
('IE:construction-manager:2026-09-12:wave-a-v1','IE:construction-manager','entry_accessibility',array['ie-construction-manager-entry-accessibility-1'],array['IE:construction-manager:entry_accessibility:wave-a-v1'],6,'career-opportunity-v4-foundation','available','proxy','medium','Official pathway evidence is converted into the frozen CampCareer Entry Accessibility rubric; the source itself does not publish a CampCareer score.','official_service','medium',0.8,'Official Level 8 Construction Management education provides a clear route, while substantial sector/project experience remains material.',null,'proxy'),
('IE:construction-manager:2026-09-12:wave-a-v1','IE:construction-manager','relative_salary',array['ie-construction-manager-relative-salary-1'],array['IE:construction-manager:relative_salary:wave-a-v1'],1.6832,'career-opportunity-v4-foundation','available','proxy','medium','CSO''s official 2022 earnings release provides the closest defensible published Pay measure at SOC major-group scope: Professional occupations. This is broader than the canonical Career and therefore Estimated evidence.','official_primary','medium',0.8,'All eight Wave A Careers map to SOC 2010 major group 2 (Professional occupations). The same broad proxy is intentionally used consistently; it must not be displayed as an exact Career salary or used to claim Pay differences within Wave A.',null,'derived'),
('IE:construction-manager:2026-09-12:wave-a-v1','IE:construction-manager','projected_growth',array['ie-construction-manager-projected-growth-1'],array['IE:construction-manager:projected_growth:wave-a-v1'],1.4833,'career-opportunity-v4-foundation','available','proxy','medium','Production & specialised services managers explicitly includes managers in construction.','government_aggregator','medium',0.8,'Production & specialised services managers explicitly includes managers in construction.',null,'derived'),
('IE:construction-manager:2026-09-12:wave-a-v1','IE:construction-manager','visa_accessibility',array['ie-construction-manager-visa-accessibility-1'],array['IE:construction-manager:visa_accessibility:wave-a-v1'],10,'career-opportunity-v4-foundation','available','proxy','medium','Official occupation-level Critical Skills eligibility is mapped into the internal CampCareer visa-accessibility rubric. This is structural Career context, not personal immigration eligibility.','official_primary','medium',0.8,'10/10 is internal pathway context only and does not contribute to CampCareer Score v1.',null,'proxy'),
('IE:construction-manager:2026-09-12:wave-a-v1','IE:construction-manager','entry_burden',array['ie-construction-manager-entry-burden-1'],array['IE:construction-manager:entry_burden:wave-a-v1'],4,'career-opportunity-v4-foundation','available','proxy','medium','Official pathway/regulation evidence is converted into the frozen CampCareer Entry Burden rubric; higher means lower burden.','official_service','medium',0.8,'No universal statutory Construction Manager register is asserted; role/site competence and construction-specific requirements still create some entry burden.',null,'proxy')
